    "updated_at": "2018-06-06T15:02:32Z",
    "body": "I understand, I was mislead by the polyfill using `JSON.parse()`. Why not extend the concept of reviver to the underlying mechanism? This would permit to instantiate JavaScript object from their JSON representation with some logic (e.g. dealing with `Date`s or returning an existing object instance where the JSON was already parsed before).\r\n",
